<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 6: </span>Control token ablations on Qwen and Mistral, deltas relative to CoT-off + no-think models. These results affirm our earlier expectations, showing that reasoning improves performance (+3.3 and +9.9 VA for Qwen and Mistral respectively) and the capability learned from reasoning training is active and controllable at inference-time. CoT-on + no-think does not recover CoT-on + think performance. </figcaption>
</figure>
