</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Synthetic reasoning text vs visual branch</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">With V1 of synthetic reasoning, we trained two models, one with answers from the text branch and one with answers from the visual branch. We find that the text branch is slightly better than the visual branch (+1.1 VA) and significantly better on MMLongBenchDoc and MMLBD-C (+2.3 and +2.0 MMLBD-C respectively). Given the changes to improve the visual branch in V2 (see §<a href="#S3.SS2" title="3.2 Trace design ‣ 3 Method ‣ Internalized Reasoning for Long-Context Visual Document Understanding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a>) and a desire to balance the visual strength of the model, we increased the portion of answers sampled from the text branch in V2 from 40% to 50%. We find it interesting that the text branch performs so well, given access to only the extracted evidence, indicating the extracted evidence contains enough information to answer questions effectively.</p>
</div>
